            <ArticleTitle>A massive occult pericardial effusion in an athletic young male.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>126-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/jramc-2013-000061</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 27-year-old Royal Marine with a massive pericardial effusion, presenting with minimal clinical findings, suggesting that high levels of physical fitness may effectively mask the normal symptoms of this potentially life-threatening condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
